  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Africa Country Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TradeMark Africa&apos;s South Africa Programme works to help Africa&apos;s most industrialised economy leverage its AfCFTA commitments and position its private sector to compete in the emerging continental market, operating under TMA&apos;s 2023&#x2013;2030 strategy with a deliberately focused remit distinct from the infrastructure-heavy programmes in other countries. The Programme centres on three interconnected priorities: supporting AfCFTA implementation by providing technical assistance to the AfCFTA Secretariat and South African firms navigating the transition to unified continental market rules, rules of origin, and dispute resolution mechanisms; accelerating digital trade transformation by addressing non-tariff barriers, including inefficient standards testing and complex customs procedures, and developing green and digital corridor solutions that capitalise on South Africa&apos;s established position as a leading hub for digitally delivered services in the region; and building industrial competitiveness in sectors with cross-border export potential under the continental free trade framework.</narrative>
  </description>
